--- !u!114 &1758467267
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1758467265}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f4688fdb7df04437aeb418b961361dc5, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Corey Polo\nLead Audio Designer [Source of Bad Cop's Ulcer]\n\nI think
    I would like to use this space to individually speak to each of my team mates
    and reflect on our work and the short journey we've started on. \n\nEmery: I
    admire your ability to balance your obligations while maintain consistent output
    of a high quality; I'm grateful for how willing and able you were to hop in,
    regardless of the domain, and help everyone out throughout production.\n\nMomo:
    I really value our conversations on our way to INT D 350. I know how you feel
    about the friction between being a 2D artist working in a 3D game, but I want
    to tell you: this game would have but a fraction of the life and character that
    it does if it didn't have your work in it. You're really talented, and I am grateful
    to have gotten to see that talent on display.\n\nBrayden: I really started to
    enjoy the level of goofiness we found in the last few weeks of the term; your
    enthusiasm is infectious and inspiring. Any time you got talking about a system
    you made, or a development you were able to get working, I found myself immediately
    excited for both you and the game. I'm looking forward to continue working together.\n\nSelena:
    I appreciate your passion and your commitment to excellence. I also really value
    the few one-on-one conversations we were able to have during the term: you're
    a thoughtful and considered person, and just stubborn enough that heated conversations
    always stay on the \"debate\" side of an argument lol. I also want to acknowledge
    something which might have gone under the radar over the term:  I noticed and
    appreciate that you very much want everyone to be at their best and do what you
    can to try and fascilitate that.  Thanks for all of your hard work!\n\nCohen:
    I'm sorry to have stressed you out so much! Our work styles are so diametrically
    opposed that I think it was bound to happen. That being said, I want you to know
    that I actually deeply appreciate your structured organizational approach and
    I know for a certainty that we wouldn't have gotten nearly the same amount done
    without it. I think that these qualities will get you very far in whatever direction
    you choose to go; they're rare! I will say, though, I never once thought of you
    as a bad cop lol. I also want you to know that through the term there were a
    few brief moments where I got to get to see non-producer Cohen and I'm looking
    forward to hopefully getting to know that side of you better. \n\nTo all of you
    (the team, not you the person reading the credits... unless of course you reading
    the credits is one of the people on the team, then yes) to all of you: THANK
    YOU! We were able to get through the term and create the first fully 3D game
    made in the game certificate program--that's a big deal! Good work, you guys
    :D I appreciate each of you <3"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0bd612f52daaa6d4c9b2b68506f8de09, type: 2}
